---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro";
import pageMeta from "@/data/page-meta.json";

const meta = pageMeta["/docs/installation/manual"];
const releaseFiles = "https://github.com/vladiantio/loseta/blob/v0.20.0/packages/loseta/registry";
---

<Layout title={meta.title} description={meta.description}>
  <div class="docs-content">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
    <h1>Manual installation</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">
      Copy loseta's CSS directly into a project without running the CLI. You own the files, the
      layer order and the markup contract.
    </p>

    <h2>Choose the files</h2>
    <p>
      This example installs the Nova button in a plain HTML project. The source links are pinned to
      <code>v0.20.0</code>; update them when you upgrade. To use another style, copy that style's
      button file instead of the Nova file.
    </p>

    <h2>Create the directory structure</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="text"
      code={`styles/loseta/
  tokens.css
  reset.css
  base.css
  utilities.css
  index.css
  components/
    button.css
  styles/
    nova/
      button.css`}
    />

    <h2>Copy the foundation</h2>
    <p>Copy the contents of each file into the matching path under <code>styles/loseta/</code>:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${releaseFiles}/tokens.css`}>tokens.css</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${releaseFiles}/reset.css`}>reset.css</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${releaseFiles}/base.css`}>base.css</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${releaseFiles}/utilities.css`}>utilities.css</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Copy the button</h2>
    <p>Button has no hard registry dependencies. Copy these two files:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href={`${releaseFiles}/components/button.css`}>components/button.css</a> — structural CSS
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={`${releaseFiles}/styles/nova/button.css`}>styles/nova/button.css</a> — Nova visual
        style
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="docs-callout" role="note">
      <strong>Adding more components.</strong> Check the component page's dependencies before
      copying files. Hard primitive dependencies need both their base CSS and the matching style
      file. Behavior-bearing components also need their declared support and entry modules.
    </div>

    <h2>Create the entrypoint</h2>
    <p>
      Create <code>styles/loseta/index.css</code> with the fixed layer order, followed by imports
      for the files you copied:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      code={`@layer loseta.tokens, loseta.reset, loseta.base, loseta.components, loseta.style, loseta.utilities;

@import "./tokens.css";
@import "./reset.css";
@import "./base.css";
@import "./utilities.css";
@import "./components/button.css";
@import "./styles/nova/button.css";`}
    />
    <p>
      Keep every source file's existing <code>@layer</code> wrapper. The generated entrypoint only
      declares the order and imports the files; it does not replace their layer blocks.
    </p>

    <h2>Load the CSS and markup</h2>
    <p>Serve the files at matching URLs and load the entrypoint from your HTML:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="html"
      code={`<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/loseta/index.css" />

<button type="button" class="btn">Button</button>`}
    />
    <p>
      No compilation or transpilation is required for the loseta files. Your static server or host
      application still needs to serve them.
    </p>

    <h2>Add behavior manually</h2>
    <p>
      Button is CSS-only. For a behavior-bearing component, copy every declared module from
      <a href={`${releaseFiles}/behaviors`}>behaviors/</a>, preserve the relative paths and load each
      entry module once. Shared modules such as <code>core.js</code> are imported by the entries.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/docs/behavior">behavior reference</a> for initialization, scoped mounting
      and the CSS-only fallback contract.
    </p>

    <h2>Use the same files in Vite or Astro</h2>
    <p>
      Place the same tree under <code>src/styles/loseta/</code> and import its entrypoint from your
      existing application stylesheet:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      code={`/* src/index.css or src/style.css */
@import "./styles/loseta/index.css";

/* src/styles/global.css */
@import "./loseta/index.css";`}
    />
    <p>
      The import path is relative to the stylesheet that contains it. Keep behavior modules in a
      source directory when importing them through the framework's module graph, or place them in
      the framework's public directory when using a root-served script.
    </p>

    <h2>Registry payload alternative</h2>
    <p>
      Every installable item is also available as JSON with inline file contents. Open the
      <a href="https://loseta.vladiantio.com/r/styles/nova/button.json">Nova button payload</a> and
      copy each <code>files[].content</code> value to its declared
      <code>files[].target</code> path. Foundation payloads live under
      <code>/r/foundation/&lt;name&gt;.json</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="https://loseta.vladiantio.com/r/registry.json">registry catalog</a> lists item
      dependencies and hashes. This path is useful for scripted extraction, but the linked source
      files are simpler for a manual install.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
